## 1. The unchanged original problem and the endpoint conclusion

This companion to [JR, §§41–57][JR], [RC, §§58–66][RC] and *Residual
height records: global quadratic certificates and actual acquisition-label
rigidity* (denoted RH) evaluates the exact NEXT endpoint value coefficient
$K_1$ and the constant correction $2K_1$ to every normalized optimal
contrast multiplier. These are finite explicit algebraic expressions.
RC already supplies the full conditional residual curve, the genuine
three-to-four-contact transition, unique grouped optima, and exact common
attainments. Those results are credited here. Sections 3–5 retain an
independent local derivation to justify the coefficient computation;
they are not a new full-curve or transition claim. Section 7 identifies
its parameter and multiplier exactly with RC's branch. Exactly four
actual low live-bearing labels are necessary and sufficient on the
proved endpoint neighborhood. This local actual-label assertion is
distinct from RC's real-atom and construction counts, and is not extended
here to a new global actual-label theorem.

